# The org signer pin: the commit of monumental-archive/signer that every
# sign.yml `uses:` in this tree points at, declared once so the release
# verifier (verify-release.yml, verdict mode) can check the provenance it
# opens was signed by the SAME tree that signed this release. GitHub
# requires `uses:` refs to be literal, so this cannot be single-sourced at
# runtime — instead lint:signer-pin asserts every literal equals this
# file, and Renovate updates both in one PR (renovate.json). A half-bump
# reddens the gate; it never verifies against a stale signer.
# renovate: signer-pin
9adecf65df19bc63a9e5576dac1b1c0c223bb514
